+
+### Autonomous scheduling and worker claims
+
+Submission is the only normal operator trigger. In the same PostgreSQL transaction that
+changes authoritative run state, the controller creates the next role-bound
+`workflow_steps` record and an outbox message. Role workers consume or poll only through a
+controller-owned claim protocol, acquire a compare-and-set expiring lease, heartbeat while
+running, and complete with content-addressed evidence plus an idempotency key. Completion
+atomically closes the current step, appends its decision/event, and schedules the next
+eligible role. A reaper returns an expired lease to the same bounded attempt or routes it
+to troubleshooting; it never invents successful output.
+
+The real proposer execution boundary invokes Wiggum with Codex as proposer and the approved
+non-interactive `compass_claude` shim as independent critic. Runtime secrets remain in the
+approved runtime environment and are never persisted in PostgreSQL, NATS, Kanban,
+ClickHouse, evidence, Compose source, or health responses. Deterministic test executors are
+allowed only behind an explicit test mode and cannot make production readiness green.
+
+The required role set is derived from the immutable specification and enabled policy.
+Readiness is fail-closed unless every required role reports a fresh heartbeat, proves its
+runtime/dependencies, and successfully claims a bounded disposable probe. The probe is
+cancelled and excluded from portfolio metrics after evidence is recorded.
